# Deliberately (almost) empty, and deliberately present.
#
# `npm pack` falls back to a package's .gitignore when there is no .npmignore -
# and this package's .gitignore excludes exactly the binary that gives the
# package its entire reason to exist. An empty .npmignore stops that fallback,
# so what ships is decided solely by the "files" allowlist in package.json.
#
# npm/smoke-test.sh asserts the packed tarball really does contain bin/lpad, so
# if this file ever goes missing the test fails rather than a hollow package
# reaching the registry.
